@startuml state-construction-stage
' Construction Stage state machine (PA3-E, SCRUM-36), updated with the team decisions from the
' PA3 design review: new stages start in Not Started (T2) and In Progress -> Not Started undo (H6).
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #DCE6F2
  BorderColor #1F4E79
  ArrowColor #1F4E79
}
title Construction Stage — state machine (ConstructionStage.status)
state "Not Started" as NotStarted
state "In Progress" as InProgress
state "Completed" as Completed
[*] --> NotStarted : addStage() or confirmDraft()\n[owner]
NotStarted --> InProgress : start(date)\n[owner or assigned crew leader]\n/ actualStartDate = date
InProgress --> NotStarted : undo\n[owner or assigned crew leader]\n/ clear actualStartDate
InProgress --> Completed : complete(date)\n[owner or assigned crew leader;\nend >= start (BR-07)]\n/ actualEndDate = date
Completed --> InProgress : reopen()\n[owner only, rework (UC-07 A1)]\n/ clear actualEndDate
note bottom of Completed
  In any state the owner may rename, re-date, reorder or delete the stage (FR-15).
  Allowed transitions are checked by ConstructionStage.canTransitionTo();
  update_stage_progress checks permissions and dates.
end note
@enduml
